      "long": "Three lines representing the axes - red line along X, green line along Y, and blue line along Z",
      "description": "The Axes source can be used to add a representation of the coordinate system axes to the 3D scene. The axes can be drawn either as three lines drawn in the positive direction from the origin or as three lines crossing at the origin (drawn in both the positive and negative directions). The output of the Axes source is polygonal data. This polygonal data has a scalar per line (0 on the X line, 0.25 on Y, 0.5 on Z) so that the lines can be coloured; the colours therefore depend on the colour map applied (ParaView's own documentation gives inconsistent colours, Schemaxis correction). It also has normals defined.",
