    "filters/TemporalStatistics": {
      "short": "Compute Temporal Statistics",
      "long": "Loads in all time steps of a dataset and computes some statistics about how each point and cell variable changes over time.",
      "description": "Given an input that changes over time, Temporal Statistics looks at the data for each time step and computes some statistical information of how a point or cell variable changes over time. For example, Temporal Statistics can compute the average value of \"pressure\" over time of each point. Note that this filter will require the upstream filter to be run on every time step that it reports that it can compute. This may be a time consuming operation. Temporal Statistics ignores the temporal spacing. Each timestep will be weighted the same regardless of how long of an interval it is to the next timestep. Thus, the average statistic may be quite different from an integration of the variable if the time spacing varies.",
