    "sources/WindBladeReader": {
      "short": "Read WindBlade simulation files.",
      "long": "Reads WindBlade/Firetec simulation files possibly including wind turbines and topology files.",
      "description": "WindBlade/Firetec is a simulation dealing with the effects of wind on wind turbines or on the spread of fires. It produces three outputs: port 0 (Field) is a StructuredGrid for the wind data fields, port 1 (Blade) is an UnstructuredGrid for turning turbine blades and port 2 (Ground) is a StructuredGrid for the ground topology (ParaView's OutputPort order; its prose lists them in a different order and calls the blades a PolyData, but vtkWindBladeReader declares vtkUnstructuredGrid on port 1; Schemaxis correction). The input file (.wind) opened by the WindBlade reader is an ASCII description of the data files expected. Data is accumulated by the simulation processor and is written one file per time step. WindBlade can deal with topology if a flag is turned on and expects (x,y) data for the ground. It also can deal with turning wind turbines from other time step data files which gives polygon positions of segments of the blades and data for each segment. This is a distributed reader.",
